{%- comment -%}
  ITM Spec Table
  --------------
  Renders raw NetSuite spec HTML ("<li>Label: value</li>" pairs) as a
  clean, centered, two-column Attribute/Value table with alternating
  white/grey rows. Parsing is shared via itm-spec-parser (the same parser
  the sortable product-group table already uses), so there's exactly one
  place that understands this raw HTML's format — this snippet only
  handles turning parsed pairs into a table.

  Used by both snippets/itm-info-accordion.liquid (the Specifications
  accordion) and sections/itm-product-html-section.liquid (the standalone
  "HTML Section" — the one actually live on real product pages, whose own
  "html" block has a "Show as table" setting).

  Params:
    raw_html (string) — required. The raw spec HTML to parse.

  Usage: {% render 'itm-spec-table', raw_html: html_output %}
  Renders nothing if there's no usable data.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign spec_raw_str = raw_html | append: ''
  capture spec_pairs
    render 'itm-spec-parser', raw_html: spec_raw_str
  endcapture
  assign spec_pairs = spec_pairs | strip
-%}
{%- if spec_pairs != '' -%}
  <table class="itm-spec-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Attribute</th>
        <th>Value</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {%- assign spec_pairs_list = spec_pairs | split: ';;' -%}
      {%- for pair in spec_pairs_list -%}
        {%- unless pair == blank -%}
          {%- assign spec_label = pair | split: '=' | first -%}
          {%- assign spec_value = pair | remove_first: spec_label | remove_first: '=' -%}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ spec_label }}</td>
            <td>{{ spec_value }}</td>
          </tr>
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </tbody>
  </table>
{%- endif -%}

<style>
  .itm-spec-table {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .itm-spec-table th,
  .itm-spec-table td {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e2e2;
  }
  .itm-spec-table th {
    font-weight: 700;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #d0d0d0;
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    A solid, clearly-visible light grey (not a barely-there foreground
    tint) — the whole point was a plain white/grey striped table like the
    reference screenshot, not something that reads as almost-white either
    way.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  .itm-spec-table tbody tr:nth-child(odd) {
    background: #f7f6f3;
  }
</style>
